2.  the khronon's own quadratic and cubic Lagrangian (flat space, decoupling limit)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    In the decoupling limit the Einstein-Hilbert term is identically zero (R = 0 for the flat metric at any
    foliation), so the WHOLE khronon Lagrangian is L = M^2 [ c_14 a.a - c_2 (div n)^2 ], M^2 = 1/(16 pi G),
    exact to all orders in chi.  Expanding tau = t + chi:
      L_2 = M^2 [ c_14 (d_i chi_dot)^2 - c_2 (lap chi)^2 ]
      L_3 = M^2 [ c_14 ( -2 chi_dot (d_i chi_dot)^2 - 2 d_i chi_dot d_j chi d_i d_j chi - 2 chi_ddot d_i chi d_i chi_dot )
                  + c_2 ( 4 lap chi d_j chi d_j chi_dot + 2 chi_dot (lap chi)^2 ) ]
  [PASS] C2a [control] the quadratic expansion of a.a and (div n)^2 is exactly (d_i chi_dot)^2 and (lap chi)^2   (exact residuals [(0, 0), (0, 0)])
  [PASS] C2b [control] the cubic expansion of a.a and (div n)^2 matches the five monomials quoted above   (exact residuals [(0, 0), (0, 0)])
    => KHRONON KINETIC NORMALISATION (flat, decoupling): the coefficient of chi_dot^2 is  2 M^2 c_14 k^2.
       Sound speed from L_2 alone: c_s^2 = c_2/c_14  (the exact value is checked in section 3).
    => EVERY cubic monomial carries the derivative multiset {1,2,2}: L_3 = M^2 c_14 (d chi)(d^2 chi)^2 uniformly.
       With the canonical field chi_c = sqrt(2 M^2 c_14) d chi this is  L_3 = chi_c (d chi_c)^2 / (2^{3/2} M sqrt(c_14)),
       a single dimension-5 operator with suppression scale  Lambda_5 = 2^{3/2} M sqrt(c_14) = 2 M_pl sqrt(c_14).
  [PASS] C2c [control] every cubic monomial has derivative multiset {1,2,2}, so L_3 is a single dim-5 operator and Lambda_5 = 2 M_pl sqrt(c_14) with no other parameter   (five monomials, derivative orders (1,2,2) each)

