7.  the screened limit: what the screening actually does to the kinetic normalisation
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The kinetic Hessian is diag(2 M^2 c_14 k^2, 2 M^2 |K_2|) at EVERY value of the screening variable: the
    AeST mixing carries one time derivative, so it is antisymmetric and drops out of the Hessian entirely.
    The screening's ONLY footprint on the frame sector is in the effective one-field description obtained
    by integrating out the stiff scalar, valid where the khronon branch is khronon-dominated:
      c_14_eff(Sigma) = c_14 + (2-K_B)/Sigma + c_2 |K_2|/[(2-K_B) Sigma]   (exact leading large-Sigma root)
    Parameters used: K_B = 0.2, c_14 = 1e-05, c_2 = c_2* = 1.00002e-05 (the alpha_2 = 0 line PPN
    forces), |K_2| = 250000.  Sigma = J_Y = s/Delta(s), the CONSERVATIVE (transverse) stiffness; the
    longitudinal one is 1/Delta'(s) = infinity on the saturated branch, for which the drag is exactly zero.

    environment                            s (can)     s (alt)         J_Y   u_khronon  |dphi_c/chi_c|    c_14_eff     /c_14
    deep MOND, galaxy outskirt                 0.1         0.1      0.3719       2.296          0.7513  4.3554e-06    0.4355  <- strongly mixed
    MOND transition                              1           1       1.718       2.296          0.7513  4.3554e-06    0.4355  <- strongly mixed
    galaxy inner disc                           10          10       15.44      2.2961          0.7513  4.3553e-06    0.4355  <- strongly mixed
    Saturn orbit (Cassini monopole)      6.898e+05   5.726e+05   1.065e+06      0.8405          0.1528  1.1898e-05    1.1898
    Earth orbit                          6.334e+07   5.258e+07   9.781e+07     0.99818        0.001617  1.0018e-05    1.0018
    Cassini conjunction, b = 1.6 R_sun   1.144e+12   9.496e+11   1.767e+12           1       8.972e-08       1e-05    1.0000

    => in the SCREENED regime the khronon branch is clean (the MOND scalar's canonical admixture is 1.62e-03 at 1 AU),
       and its effective normalisation is c_14_eff = 1.00184e-05 = c_14 x 1.00184 at 1 AU, 1.18979 at Saturn, 1.0000001 at Cassini conjunction.
    => the screening does not multiply the normalisation: it REMOVES a positive correction to it. The
       correction falls as a POWER LAW 1/J_Y ~ Delta/s, not as the exponential e^{-y} A3 asks for, and it
       is +0.184% of c_14 at 1 AU and +0.00001% at Cassini conjunction.
    => in the UNSCREENED rows the khronon is NOT a separate mode: the canonical admixture is O(1), and the
       'c_14_eff' there is a mixed clock-scalar quantity, not a khronon normalisation. Reported, not used.
  [PASS] P4 [P7 mechanism] the screened-limit kinetic normalisation is NOT below the bare floor c_14, i.e. the screening does not multiply the normalisation by a vanishing factor   (current action: c_14_eff/c_14 = 1.00184 >= 1 at 1 AU (the screening removes a POSITIVE correction). Discriminating: the historical eta = 2 e^{-y} action gives eta/c_14 = 10^{-2.75e+07} there, which is what P7 was written about)
  [PASS] P5 [P7 escape clause] an INDEPENDENT FINITE NORMALISATION exists in the screened limit   (c_14_eff -> c_14 = 1e-05 exactly; the exact kinetic Hessian 2 M^2 c_14 k^2 carries NO screening variable at any Sigma)

