9.  what the screening DOES cost: the MOND scalar's cone, and what the published action does not define
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The MOND scalar's kinetic normalisation is |K_2| (constant) but its gradient stiffness is J_Y = s/Delta(s),
    which the static law forces to grow linearly with s.  Its sound speed is therefore FORCED:
        c_s,perp^2 = (2-K_B) J_Y c^2 / |K_2|  >=  (2-K_B) s c^2 / (C |K_2|),   C = Delta_max = 0.6476
